 Authoritative rules: `SWWEB-*`.
 
 ## Verified Facts
+
+- Billing-aware balances and displayed charge lines use App's BillingType.signedAmount: adjustment subtracts the quantity-scaled subtotal; other billing types add it. Initial order loading, refresh, SOC budget import, charge edits, trip balances, order/POS prints and sales detail/history summaries share this direction. Locally appended order/trip records retain raw prices; only calculation/display values are signed, preventing double negation. Charge/service/budget forms preserve adjustment classification from the actual SOC code. Budget ItemView and SalePointObject retain local billingType with charge defaults; new/loaded service rows derive it from ChargeObject or the loaded CustSOC, cart copies preserve it, and budget/cart/edited/historic totals apply it. Shared payload prices remain raw. The user's corrected StartServiceOrder.calcBalance is unchanged. Product/rental/payment-only values and report DTOs without a discriminator are not reclassified. Source-audited; builds/tests/browser verification remains unrun for this change.
 
 - OrderView compact presentation binds a highlighted folio to `AccoutOverview.$order` beside Cuenta / Órdenes and hides it outside a loaded order. The existing state-colored status selector/menu now sits on the priority/alert row in a 32px pill with 16px text; existing permissions, actions and hidden options remain intact. Equipment inspection uses ten native checkboxes bound to the original check/disabled states, while prepared/delivered rental controls are unchanged. Configurable tag1/tag2 (Marca/Modelo) share a responsive row; diagnosis/resolution add actions use 14px text. Service-letter/contract headers show decorative blue SVGs, and the address header has a blue map SVG with left-aligned text. The inset holder and floating corner icon stay unchanged. Source-audited; browser rendering and new build verification remain pending.
 - `TripViewBeta` adds an Entrega column: only multi-item in-progress trips offer Entregar for undelivered linked commercial assets. `FiscalMercanciaItem.deliverd` supplies the Entregado marker on every trip size; canceled final movements use Movimiento finalizado. The delivery initializer of `ConfirmTripStatusUpdate` reuses one-item comments, local uploads, remote camera and gallery evidence, blocks confirmation during pending image uploads, and validates linked routes/unique safe filenames. The parent serializes status/delivery mutations and owns one popup, closes it on removal, checks session/trip/asset/snapshot response identities, then applies only the confirmed item flag and returned trip status (including auto-completion), notifies the dashboard/caller and refreshes trip/notes. Generation and confirmed-item checks reject stale refreshes. Optional destination section/subsection are omitted by this UI. App target compilation verified with the updated shared packages; browser/mobile/server behavior remains unverified.
